[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1384","stub":{"id":"1384","section":"Tuxedo to Suffern","altname":"","river":"Ramapo","difficulty":"ItoIIstandoutVplus","states":["USA-NYO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"75","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"portage","description":"A dam and a Waterfalls at site of the former augusta furnace. Lousy portages on either side. Eroded trails, drops, prickle bushes.\n\nThe falls (CL5 or CL6, I don't know, you decide. Run at your own risk. A paddler more experienced than me believes the landing may be too shallow.)","id":"107296","location":{"latitude":"41.20162","longitude":"-74.183789"},"name":"Augusta Furnace","distance":"-0.5","photoID":"40096","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112185","location":{"latitude":"41.195789","longitude":"-74.183605"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"Toughest real rapids on the river. Barely class 2, but does require a move around a boulder mid rapid. Sort of a surfing spot at the bottom. Can be accessed by parking at the end of Lincoln Lane and paddling across the lake.\n\nExit from the lake is a left turn that catches wood and often has a squirt line.","id":"107297","location":{"latitude":"41.176483","longitude":"-74.186068"},"name":"Drop into Lincoln Street Lake","distance":"1.42","photoID":"0","difficulty":"II","approximate":false},{"type":"playspot","description":"Remains of another old dam above washington ave has about a 1' drop with surfing potential that never seems to be realized. ok access from  east side of washington ave bridge. Pretty spot with obvious fisherman parking.","id":"107298","location":{"latitude":"41.168504","longitude":"-74.190825"},"name":"Another old dam above Washington Ave.","distance":"2","difficulty":"I","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"portage","description":"Portage on right. About a 6' drop into a lot of rip rap with a lot of wood. Has been run.","id":"107299","location":{"latitude":"41.195789","longitude":"-74.183605"},"name":"Sloatsburg Dam aka Ramapo Falls","distance":"2.9","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"portage","description":"This one is pretty obvious and can be quite a hazard for beginners. The dam blew out on the left side and you'll see a pretty high concrete dam that looks like it crossed the river. Holds wood and the river  pushes pretty hard against the dam which has a lip that comes into play.\n\nHolds wood that at times has been pretty awkward and seldom visible from the river - in the main flow which is pretty powerful here.\n\nBeginners should scout/portage  by pulling out on river left on sandbars above the dam. Skilled paddlers who are unchallenged so far can probably stick to the inside.\n\nCan be scouted from a school bus turnaround on 17 north immediately after the thruway bridge. With no leaves you get a pretty good view.","id":"107300","location":{"latitude":"41.140439","longitude":"-74.172332"},"name":"Another Old Dam","distance":"4.7","photoID":"0","difficulty":"II","approximate":false},{"type":"hazard","description":"Island around community center has had some really awkward wood that's been a big issue for the aspiring beginners that often run this. Left usually looks more enticing but has been undercutting the bank. Beginners - be careful and if in doubt get out. There's enough flow to make things bad here.","id":"107301","location":{"latitude":"41.138383","longitude":"-74.163732"},"name":"Community Center Island","distance":"4.75","photoID":"0","difficulty":"II","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Nice pull out for those with 2 cars. Pretty little park that is popular with locals on nice summer days.","id":"107302","location":{"latitude":"41.135074","longitude":"-74.163497"},"name":"Flat Rock drop/pull out","distance":"5.5","photoID":"0","difficulty":"I","approximate":false},{"type":"portage","description":"Portage on right","id":"107303","location":{"latitude":"41.126893","longitude":"-74.165055"},"name":"Substation dam","distance":"6.15","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Pullout under railroad bridge of below (but above sewage treatment plant). Carry across fields. Closest drivable access is usually at south end of fields. 80-150 yard carry depending on access.","id":"107304","location":{"latitude":"41.114274","longitude":"-74.157516"},"name":"Ball Field pullout and parking","distance":"7.2","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"40100","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9025","description":"","caption":"40100.jpeg","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40100","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40100"}},{"id":"40093","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9026","description":" This is the first tier. The little low-head dam action at the top is about a 6 to 12 inches high, no a concern at this level. If I was standing on that be rock, I would not be able to see over. I guess the first drop is about seven feet. I guess at this level you could drop down, set up and run the secound half. I bet at higher levels you'll have to keep going but I'm just guessing. ","caption":"ramapo fall","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40093","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40093"}},{"id":"881938","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"884598","description":"Rapids below tuxedo falls. ","caption":"Rapids below tuxedo falls. ","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/881938","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/881938"}},{"id":"VxAbAntGkiu3MtFO3IlHI","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Sv1W9qhra26j45afe5pln","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Marty Plante","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2022-04-17T19:15:17.000Z","updated_at":"2024-04-12T19:15:17.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/VxAbAntGkiu3MtFO3IlHI","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/VxAbAntGkiu3MtFO3IlHI"}},{"id":"891523","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895411","description":null,"caption":null,"poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891523","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891523"}},{"id":"pWyT49sr20KRhrIhqFiCL","ext":"jpg","post_id":"I4cqmQBmSGylAtEW4FFPK","description":null,"caption":"Ramapo @Tuxedo to Suffern","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Marty Plante","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2022-04-18T01:10:41.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/pWyT49sr20KRhrIhqFiCL","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/pWyT49sr20KRhrIhqFiCL"}},{"id":"tQSoBMz3Ij1p6emRif6D9","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Sv1W9qhra26j45afe5pln","description":"Steve Ferder on the Ramapo River","caption":"Steve Ferder on the Ramapo River","poi_name":null,"subject":"Steve Ferder on the Ramapo River","author":"Marty Plante","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2022-04-17T19:15:17.000Z","updated_at":"2024-04-12T19:15:17.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/tQSoBMz3Ij1p6emRif6D9","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/tQSoBMz3Ij1p6emRif6D9"}},{"id":"YIWUE5PMGYQmE7QCA2Ttt","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Sv1W9qhra26j45afe5pln","description":"Eileen Yin on the Ramapo River rapids.","caption":"Eileen Yin on the Ramapo River rapids.","poi_name":null,"subject":"Eileen Yin on the Ramapo River rapids.","author":"Marty Plante","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2022-04-17T19:15:17.000Z","updated_at":"2024-04-12T19:15:17.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/YIWUE5PMGYQmE7QCA2Ttt","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/YIWUE5PMGYQmE7QCA2Ttt"}},{"id":"40096","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9025","description":" This is what you will be running if you drop down on river right. CL6? The left of center looks very doable, the right side, I donno. It reminded me of Dead Horse on Bulls Bridge. I took this shot from a rock I climbed up on.","caption":"Falls, river-right","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40096","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40096"}},{"id":"40091","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9025","description":"A two tiered waterfall, CL5(?) in the background, the slide in the forground. AT 320 the river right was too shallow to run but at higher water it will be a sneak. Center, just left of the rock was runnable.  Go right to avoid the hole, center you're running the hole left of that there's a rooster-tail, nature/cause unknown to me. All the way left was too shallow too run. I could not see what hazards lurked on river left but it looked like it was a # of small drops.  ","caption":"Ramapo Falls","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40091","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40091"}}],"detail":{"id":"1384","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"With the exception of the a few questionable drops, this is a beginning whitewater run from Tuxedo on down, with the advantage of a train or bus shuttle.\n\nThe river below 7 Lakes Drive is the shallowest part between Tuxedo and Sloatburg and becomes too scrapy somewhere around 300 cfs.\n\nDownstream from here, before you pass under 7 Lakes Drive just upstream of a bridge (Washington Ave?), there was a surf-hole. At higher levels this might get really good since the river is constricted here. It looks like there might have been an old rustic dam here. Soon you will pass under 7 Lakes Drive; you can take out here.\n\nStony Brook will pour in from your left after passing under 7 Lakes Drive and the water will go dead flat. This is due to the Dam. It's a low-head dam, however, there's something in there to stop the recirc but all the way left has recirc and probably other spots as well. I ran just left of the recirc, right of the log sticking up. The rocks seem like they have good pin potential and there's junk in this dam. This is the last CL3 I know about.\n\nBelow Sloatsburg, there's a section where the scenery is not great after this and you'll hear and see the Thruway. There may be parking on Waldron Terrace near the dam which can be accessed by taking 7 Lakes Drive. Make a right on Waldron and drive until you see the signs 'Do not pass'; the dam is on you right.\n\n**[Google Map of New York Whitewater](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zjdnDE8H0TLg.kJnMWGapL4xk)**","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"7.3","correlations":[{"reachID":"1384","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"200","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"3000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"RAMAPO RIVER AT SUFFERN NY","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01387420","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","late